# === Imported designs (design/handoff/) ===
# No ignore rule on purpose. /design-handoff unzips a Claude Design export or a
# Design artifact's files into design/handoff/<slug>/bundle/ and keeps reference
# images in screens/; the snapshot is committed so a session without the Claude
# Design connector or the Figma MCP server can still read what was designed.
# `*.zip` above is intentionally NOT re-included here: the bundle is committed
# unzipped, never as an archive. A local .fig copy stays out too (see the Large
# Binary Media block) -- the live Figma file is the source.
# The unanchored rules above (`dist/`, `build/`, `out/`, `bin/`, `examples/`,
# `node_modules/`, `*.log`, `.env`) match at any depth, so they silently drop
# those parts of a bundle. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so no negation is added; /design-handoff runs `git check-ignore`
# on the snapshot and reports every dropped file in the record's
# `## Ignored or Dropped Files`.

# === Retained QA evidence (keep last) ===
# Evidence only counts when it is committed. The generic `*.log` and `*.zip`
# rules above would silently drop a story's migration-dry-run.log and its
# Playwright trace archives, so both are re-included under the evidence tree.
!production/qa/evidence/**/*.log
!production/qa/evidence/**/*.zip
